    "post_id": 67649,
    "title": "שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר בָּנִים | Shném 'Asar Banim — a shiv’ata cycle for Musaf on the Shabbat of a bat mitsvah, by Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "author": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "coauthors": [
        {
            "name": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
            "bio": "From a family of musicians, Isaac Gantwerk Mayer believes that creative art is one of the most powerful ways to get in touch with the divine. He composes music and poetry in Hebrew and English. (He also <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=342\">translates</a> and <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=820\">transcribes</a> Hebrew and Aramaic texts, adding <em>niqqud</em> and <em>t'amim</em> as needed.) Isaac runs a Jewish music transcription service, which will transcribe and set any Jewish music in any language, recorded or written. Contact his service on <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pg/isaacgmayerjewishtranscription/\">Facebook</a> or via <a href=\"https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com/contact\">his music blog</a>.",
            "website": "https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/isaac-gantwerk-mayer-2021-e1674561264977-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/isaac-gantwerk-mayer"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-06-04",
    "last_updated": "2026-06-26",
    "excerpt": "A shiv’ata is a sevenfold blessing inserted into the Musaf service on Shabbat. This original shiv’ata is for a bat mitsvah following the traditional count, where a girl turns twelve. Each stanza begins with an example of twelve as used in our tradition, followed by an alphabetical acrostic.",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\nA <em>shiv’ata</em> is a sevenfold blessing inserted into the Musaf service on Shabbat. This original shiv’ata is for a bat mitsvah following the traditional count, where a girl turns twelve. Each stanza begins with an example of twelve as used in our tradition, followed by an alphabetical acrostic. A companion piyyuṭ for a bar mitsvah, when a boy turns thirteen, can be found <a href=\"/?p=67620\">here</a>.</p>\n<p>Note: “<span class=\"divine-referent\">The CAUSE</span>” is used to translate the Divine Name <span class=\"divine-referent\">YHVH</span>, based on the philosophical idea of <span class=\"divine-referent\">God</span> as the <span class=\"divine-referent\">Prime Mover</span> and on the interpretation of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Name</span> as a causative form of the copula – “causes to be.” This translation also uses the plural pronouns <span class=\"divine-referent\">They</span>/<span class=\"divine-referent\">Their</span>/<span class=\"divine-referent\">Them</span> to refer to <span class=\"divine-referent\">God</span> as a <em>pluralis majestatis</em>, and to avoid the implications of <span class=\"divine-referent\">God</span> being assigned a gender. (Find Ibn Ezra’s commentary on Genesis 1:1 for a discussion of the <em>pluralis majestatis</em> when referring to <span class=\"divine-referent\">God</span>.) All divine referents (pronouns, epithets, names) are rendered in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicase\">unicase</a>.\n</div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Hebrew)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשְׁנֵים עָשָׂר בָּנִים <span class=\"acrostic\">אַ</span>חַת הִיא הַיּוֹנָה<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">בָּ</span>נוֹת רָאֽוּהָ וַיְאַשְּׁרֽוּהָ בְּרִנָּה<br />\nבְּיוֹם בַּת מִצְוָתָהּ <span class=\"acrostic\">גִּ</span>דְּלָה כִּי בָאָה עוֹנָה<br />\nוַתֹּ֖אמֶר <span class=\"acrostic\">דָּ</span>תִי וְדִינֵי אֲקַבֵּל כְּאִמּוֹת הַשּׁוֹשַׁנָּה׃<br />\nבא״י מָגֵן אַבְרָהָם׃<br />\nאַתָּה גִּבּוֹר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nTwelve sons; one is the dove.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> A dual meaning, referring to Song of Songs 6:9 (as does the next verse) but also to the fact that Jacob had twelve sons and one daughter.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nThe daughters see her and call her content in cheer. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn this one’s bat mitsvah day, she has grown, for the time has come, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nand she said,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> The opening word of the last line of each stanza comes from Ruth 3:6&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> &#8220;My faith and law I accept like the mothers of the rose.”<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Referring to the matriarchs. “The rose” is a poetic term for Israel.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Cause</span>, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Shield of Abraham</span>.<br />\nYou are mighty…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשְׁנֵים עָשָׂר שְׁבָטִים <span class=\"acrostic\">הֶ</span>עֱבַֽרְתָּ בַּיָּם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">וְ</span>אָז תָּשִׁיר עִם־אַחֶֽיהָ מִרְיָם<br />\nבְּיוֹם בַּת מִצְוָתָהּ <span class=\"acrostic\">זְ</span>כוּיוֹת הַמִּצְוֺת בְּמִלּוּיָם<br />\nאֵלֶ֑יהָ <span class=\"acrostic\">חַ</span>יִּים מֵימֵי אֵל חַי וְקַיָּם׃<br />\nבא״י מְחַיֵּה הַמֵּתִים׃<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">אשכנז</span> נַעֲרִיצְךָ/ <span class=\"instruction\">ספרד</span> כֶּֽתֶר…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nTwelve tribes You made pass in the sea, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nand thus Miriam sang with her brothers. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn this one’s bat mitsvah day, the merits of the commandments in their filling are <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nto her, living are the waters of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the living and enduring Deity</span>. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Cause</span>, who revives the dead.<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">Ashkenaz:</span> Let’s exult in You… <span class=\"instruction\">Sefarad:</span> A crown…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשְׁנֵים עָשָׂר מַזָּלוֹת <span class=\"acrostic\">טַ</span>בַּעְתָּם בִּרְקִיעָם<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">יִ</span>שְׂרָאֵל שׁוֹמֵֽעַ קוֹל אֵל (<span class=\"instruction\">שבת שובה –</span> מֶּֽלֶךְ) רָם וְרַֽעַם<br />\nבְּיוֹם בַּת מִצְוָתָהּ <span class=\"acrostic\">כִּ</span>תְרֵי תּוֹרַת קׇדְשְׁךָ תֵּן־לָהּ מִטַּֽעַם<br />\nכֹּ֛ל <span class=\"acrostic\">לִ</span>קְחָהּ טוֹב וּדְרָכֶֽיהָ דַּרְכֵי־נֹֽעַם׃<br />\nבא״י הָאֵל (<span class=\"instruction\">שבת שובה –</span> הַמֶּֽלֶךְ)  הַקָּדוֹשׁ׃<br />\nתִּכַּֽנְתָּ…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nTwelve zodiac signs; their ring is in their firmament. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nIsrael hears the voice of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Deity</span> (<span class=\"instruction\">on Shabbat Shuvah:</span> <span class=\"divine-referent\">Sovereign</span>), exalted and thundering. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn this one’s bat mitsvah day, the crowns of Your holy Torah<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> On the day the Torah was given, the angels gave Israel two crowns.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> grant her, because <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nall its teachings are good, and its paths are pleasant paths.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[5]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Proverbs 4:2 and 3:17, recited at the end of the Torah service.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Cause</span>, <span class=\"divine-referent\">the holy Deity</span> (<span class=\"instruction\">on Shabbat Shuvah:</span> <span class=\"divine-referent\">Sovereign</span>)<br />\nYou established…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשְׁנֵים עָשָׂר חֳדָשִׁים <span class=\"acrostic\">מִ</span>נִּיסָן עַד־אֲדָר<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">נִ</span>תַּן רֹאשָׁם לְנָשִׁים בְּהוֹד וְהָדָר<br />\nבְּיוֹם בַּת מִצְוָתָהּ <span class=\"acrostic\">שַׂ</span>מְּחָהּ בַּיּוֹם הַמֻּגְדָּר<br />\nאֲשֶׁר־<span class=\"acrostic\">עֳ</span>נָגָיו יוֹצְאִים מִשֶּׁבַּקֹּדֶשׁ נֶאְדָּר<br />\nבא״י מְקַדֵּשׁ הַשַּׁבָּת׃<br />\nרְצֵה…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nTwelve months from Nisan to Adar, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\ntheir first-day given to women<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[6]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Rosh Ḥodesh, the new moon, has long been in many mystical circles a holiday of women. The original reasoning for this was probably biological, but many other spiritual explanations have been suggested over the years.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> in splendor and splendiferousness <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn this one’s bat mitsvah day, make her rejoice on the delineated day<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[7]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> The Sabbath&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nthat has pleasures deriving from <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Awesome in Holiness</span>! <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Cause</span>, who sanctifies the sabbath.<br />\nDesire…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשְׁתֵּים עֶשְׂרֵה מַצֵּבוֹת <span class=\"acrostic\">פּ</span>וֹנוֹת הַר הַתִּפְאֶֽרֶת<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">צ</span>וֹפְפוּ בְּיַד צוֹפֶה לְשַׁמֵּשׁ כְּתִזְכֹּֽרֶת<br />\nבְּיוֹם בַּת מִצְוָתָהּ <span class=\"acrostic\">ק</span>וֹרֵא אָבִֽיהָ וְאִמָּהּ אוֹמֶֽרֶת<br />\nתֹּאמְרִ֥י <span class=\"acrostic\">רְ</span>צוֹנִי לִשְׁמֹר מִשְׁמֶֽרֶת׃<br />\nבא״י הַמַּחֲזִיר שְׁכִינָתוֹ לְצִיּוֹן׃<br />\nמוֹדִים…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nTwelve pillars facing the Mount of Glory<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[8]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Exodus 24:4&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nwere brought together by the watcher<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[9]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Moses&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> to serve as a reminder. <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn this one’s bat mitsvah day, her father calls, and her mother says, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n“You may say: ‘my desire is to keep the watch.’” <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Cause</span>, who returns <span class=\"divine-referent\">Their</span> <span class=\"divine-referent\">presence</span> to Ẓíōn.<br />\nWe thank…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשְׁתֵּים עֶשְׂרֵה אַבְנֵי <span class=\"acrostic\">שֹֽׁ</span>הַם אַבְנֵי מִלּוּאִים<br />\n<span class=\"acrostic\">שְׁ</span>מוֹת הַשְּׁבָטִים וְנִדְבוֹת הַנְּשִׂיאִים<br />\nבְּיוֹם בַּת מִצְוָתָהּ <span class=\"acrostic\">תּ</span>וֹדוֹת תּוֹדֶה לְעֹשֵׂה פְּלָאִים<br />\nאֵלַ֖י <span class=\"acrostic\">תָּ</span>רַֽמְתָּ אָז טוּבְךָ אָֽנוּ קוֹרְאִים׃<br />\nבא״י הַטּוֹב שִׁמְךָ וּלְךָ נָאֶה לְהוֹדוֹת׃<br />\nשִׂים…\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nTwelve stones of onyx, stones to be set, <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nthe names of the tribes and the donations of the princes.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[10]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Find Exodus 35:27&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nOn this one’s bat mitsvah day she will thank thanks to <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Wonderworker</span>: <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\n“To me You have contributed! Thus Your goodness we call.” <span class=\"acrostic\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Cause</span>, whose name is <span class=\"divine-referent\">good</span>, to You it is pleasing to praise.<br />\nGrant…\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nשְׁתֵּים עֶשְׂרֵה שָׁנִים יַׄלְדַּת צִׄיּוֹן חׄוֹגֶֽגֶת קִׄדּוּמָהּ<br />\nהִׄיא רְׄאוּיַת אֵׄל לָׄהּ נָתָן הַגְשָׁמָה<br />\nבְּיוֹם בַּת מִצְוָתָהּ חִׄזְׄקִׄי אִׄמְׄצִׄי וְקִרְאִי לִפְנֵי הָאֻמָּה<br />\nאֶׄעֱשֶֽׂה מִׄצְוֺת נׄוֹרָא כִּי אֶהְיֶה לְעַלְמָה׃<br />\nבא״י הַמְבָרֵךְ אֶת־עַמּוֹ יִשְׂרָאֵל בַּשָּׁלוֹם׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nTwelve years Ẓíōn’s daughter celebrates her advancement.<br />\nShe is worthy of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Deity</span>, who gives her fulfillment.<br />\nOn this one’s bat mitsvah day, be strong! Be courageous! And say before the nation,<br />\n“I will do the commandments of <span class=\"divine-referent\">the Awesome One</span>, as I become a young woman.”<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[11]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Though often mistranslated in Christian circles, the word <em>almah</em> has no connotations of sexual status whatsoever in Hebrew, referring to any young unmarried adult woman.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nBlessed are You, <span class=\"divine-referent\">Cause</span>, who blesses <span class=\"divine-referent\">Their</span> people Israel in peace.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class=\"speaker-mute footnotes_reference_container\"> <div class=\"footnote_container_prepare\"><p><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_label pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\">Notes</span><span role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_reference_container_collapse_button\" style=\"display: none;; display: none;\" onclick=\"footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1();\"></span></p></div> <div id=\"footnote_references_container__1\" style=\"\"><table class=\"footnotes_table footnote-reference-container\"><caption class=\"accessibility\">Notes</caption> <tbody> \r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >1</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">A dual meaning, referring to Song of Songs 6:9 (as does the next verse) but also to the fact that Jacob had twelve sons and one daughter.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >2</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">The opening word of the last line of each stanza comes from Ruth 3:6</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >3</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Referring to the matriarchs. “The rose” is a poetic term for Israel.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >4</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">On the day the Torah was given, the angels gave Israel two crowns.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >5</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find Proverbs 4:2 and 3:17, recited at the end of the Torah service.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >6</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Rosh Ḥodesh, the new moon, has long been in many mystical circles a holiday of women. The original reasoning for this was probably biological, but many other spiritual explanations have been suggested over the years.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >7</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">The Sabbath</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >8</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find Exodus 24:4</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >9</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Moses</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >10</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Find Exodus 35:27</td></tr>\r\n\r\n<tr class=\"footnotes_plugin_reference_row\"> <th scope=\"row\" id=\"footnote_plugin_reference__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_index pointer\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToAnchor__1('footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11');\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"footnote_plugin_link\" >11</a></th> <td class=\"footnote_plugin_text\">Though often mistranslated in Christian circles, the word <em>almah</em> has no connotations of sexual status whatsoever in Hebrew, referring to any young unmarried adult woman.</td></tr>\r\n\r\n </tbody> </table> </div></div><script type=\"text/javascript\"> function footnote_expand_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').show(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('−'); } function footnote_collapse_reference_container__1() { jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').hide(); jQuery('#footnote_reference_container_collapse_button__1').text('+'); } function footnote_expand_collapse_reference_container__1() { if (jQuery('#footnote_references_container__1').is(':hidden')) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); } else { footnote_collapse_reference_container__1(); } } function footnote_moveToReference__1(p_str_TargetID) { footnote_expand_reference_container__1(); var l_obj_Target = jQuery('#' + p_str_TargetID); if (l_obj_Target.length) { jQuery( 'html, body' ).delay( 0 ); jQuery('html, body').animate({ scrollTop: l_obj_Target.offset().top - window.innerHeight * 0.2 }, 380); } } function footnote_moveTo